<title>TURKEY: Turkish wholesale prices rise 6.0 pct in March.</title>
<headline>Turkish wholesale prices rise 6.0 pct in March.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's wholesale prices rose 6.0 percent month-on-month in March after a rise of 6.2 percent in February, the State Institute of Statistics said on Friday.</p>
<p>It said March consumer prices rose 5.4 percent, compared with a rise of 5.7 percent the previous month.  </p>
<p>Year-on-year wholesale inflation was up 77.0 percent in March, after a rise of 78.6 percent in February, it said.</p>
<p>The year-on-year consumer price rise was 77.3 in March, compared with 77.7 percent a month earlier.</p>
<p> TURKISH PRICES		 Mar 97    Mar 96    Feb 97  Jan 97</p>
<p>Wholesale mo/mo pct change    6.0	 7.0	 6.2	 5.6</p>
<p>Wholesale yr/yr		  77.0	72.1	78.6	78.0</p>
<p>Wholesale index (1994=100)  490.7     277.3     462.8     435.8</p>
<p>Consumer mo/mo pct change     5.4	 5.6	 5.7	5.9</p>
<p>Consumer yr/yr		   77.3	80.9	77.7	75.7</p>
<p>Consumer index (1994=100)   507.8     286.4     481.8     456.0</p>
